{"decision":"edit","issues":[{"quote":"Two upright metallic coil springs stand on a pale, finely textured surface, each rising from a dark circular ring marking that remains fixed beneath it.","problem":"At the start the springs are above the ring markings and are not clearly standing or rising from them; they also lean rather than being simply upright."},{"quote":"the lower turns stay near the surface","problem":"The lower coils initially descend toward the surface; the frames do not show them staying near the surface throughout."},{"quote":"each swaying and tilting through a modest oscillating lean","problem":"No clear oscillating sway is visible; the lean changes gradually as the springs slump and compress."},{"quote":"Their base contact points hold roughly the same horizontal positions above the ring markings.","problem":"Base contact points are not clearly established throughout the excerpt; the visible relation is that the lower ends remain roughly aligned with the ring markings."}],"caption":"Two metallic coil springs settle toward a pale, finely textured surface, each above a dark circular ring marking fixed on the surface. A blurred teal-green backdrop fills the upper view behind a soft curved horizon. Already mid-process, the springs hold tall, open coils and lean slightly as they settle downward.

As the motion advances, both springs shorten vertically: the upper coils descend toward the lower turns, and the spacing between successive coils steadily narrows. The two springs behave alike but not in lockstep, each gradually changing its lean as the top shifts sideways relative to its base. Their lower ends remain roughly aligned with the ring markings. Meanwhile the curved horizon and the spring bases drift downward, a slow camera tilt superimposed on the settling motion.

By the later moments the springs are markedly slumped and tilted, their coils packed tighter than at the start, yet the compression is still underway rather than resolved.","length_note":""}
